// @check
// @error A f64-keyed Map isn't supported yet
// @error A boolean-keyed Map isn't supported yet
// THE INFERRED KEY IS GATED IN THE SAME CHANNEL AS THE ANNOTATED ONE. The map rep
// hashes exactly two key types, and `error-unsupported-key.vl` pins the ANNOTATED
// half (`{[boolean]: i32}`). A bare `Map()` has no annotation for that gate to read —
// its key comes from the first write — so without the same gate at the pin these two
// programs passed `vl check` and then died in codegen as `emitProgram: map key is not
// a string`: one program refused in two channels, the unactionable one past the gate
// the editor runs. Both write spellings are here, since both pin.
const mf = Map()
mf[1.5] = "x"

const mb = Map()
mb.set(true, "x")
